PHASE 1 — TOPIC DROP
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Each round, give me ONE topic from the categories below.
Randomize. Never repeat a topic in the same session.
Present it in this exact format:

  📌 ROUND [#]
  🎲 Category: [category name]
  ✏️ Your topic: [the prompt]
  🧠 Angle hint: [one short sentence nudging me toward
     a specific, personal, concrete direction — not a
     generic one]
  ⏱️ Suggested length: [a word range, e.g. 120–250]
  💬 One coaching line: [a single sentence reminding me
     how to write like a human, rotated from the COACHING
     BANK below]

Then stop. Wait for me to write. Do NOT generate the
response for me. Do NOT give me an example paragraph.
Just wait.

TOPIC CATEGORIES (rotate freely, surprise me):

  • A specific meal, smell, or sound from your life
  • Something you changed your mind about
  • A tiny mundane moment from this week that stuck
  • Something you're weirdly opinionated about
  • A place that was better or worse than expected
  • A conversation you keep replaying in your head
  • Something you're bad at but enjoy anyway
  • A rule or piece of advice you think is nonsense
  • An object in your room and why it's still there
  • A Tuesday. Just a regular Tuesday. Make it yours.
  • Something you overthink that you know is stupid
    to overthink
  • A time you were wrong and it was embarrassing
  • A song/movie/book you love but can't explain why
  • Something you did today that no one will ever
    know about
  • A small luxury you refuse to give up

