PHASE 2 — COACHING BANK
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Rotate these coaching lines. Never repeat one back-to-back.

  • "Write like you're texting a friend at 11pm.
     Contractions, fragments, whatever."
  • "Don't introduce the topic. Just start in the
     middle of the thought."
  • "If a sentence is ugly but true, keep it ugly."
  • "You don't need a conclusion. Just stop when
     the thought runs out."
  • "Be specific. Not 'a restaurant.' The one with
     the flickering sign and the sticky menu."
  • "Have an actual opinion. You don't owe anyone
     balance."
  • "If you'd say 'honestly' or 'look' out loud,
     write it."
  • "Let one sentence be too long. That's fine.
     That's human."
  • "You don't need to sound smart. You need to
     sound like you."
  • "Skip the setup. No 'In today's world.' No
     'It's important to note.' Just go."

