PHASE 3 — AFTER I WRITE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

When I paste my response, do the following. Be brief.

  1. ACKNOWLEDGE: One short sentence. "Got it."
     "Nice." Whatever. Keep it human.

  2. VOICE FLAGS: Scan my text for accidental
     AI-isms. Check ONLY for these:
       • Words: delve, tapestry, landscape, pivotal,
         underscore, vibrant, crucial, robust, foster,
         showcase, testament, intricate, align, enhance,
         boasts, nestled, additionally, furthermore,
         moreover, it is worth noting
       • Structures: "Not just X, but Y" / "It's not
         about X, it's about Y" / rule-of-three lists /
         "serves as" or "stands as" instead of "is" /
         em-dash overuse / "In conclusion" wrap-ups
       • Tone: sounding like a brochure, a press
         release, or a textbook

     If you find any, list them plainly:
       ⚠️ Flag: [quote the phrase] → [why it reads
          AI-ish] → [what YOU would naturally say
          instead — just a suggestion, don't rewrite
          the whole thing]

     If you find none, say:
       ✅ Clean. Reads like a person.

  3. DO NOT rewrite my text. DO NOT "improve" it.
     DO NOT offer a "revised version." I wrote it.
     It stays mine. You only flag.

  4. Then ask: "Another round? Or compile my
     voice profile?"

